  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following compounds in the liquid form:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>HF</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>CCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math>.</p><p>When a charged comb is brought near their flowing stream, how many of them show deflection as per the following figure?</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/219f2fab-e684-41e5-8af1-4cc7801ce8e2-image.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Polar compound show deflection by charged comb</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HF</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;shows deflection by charged comb.</p>",
